    {
      "id": "eacf5447-2579-4399-b31f-48fbedaf9fe2",
      "text": "The Nepalese currency is the coolest. Each bill has a different animal on it.\n\nAnyways, I was on the hunt for a traditional breakfast this morning. Apparently it's not common to have breakfast in Nepal, but there are still some mid-morning snacks people have. I walked 20 minutes outside the touristy Thamel to find a little open restaurant where I got Sel roti (a deep fried rice donut), tarkari (a chickpea curry soup), and a masala chai ($0.92 total). In search of Wifi, I later ended up at a cafe and got a milk tea. The server was a very kind college-aged kid.",
      "type": "text"
    },
