    {
      "id": "cffc2576-340c-4a11-ad81-bc72f541cfaf",
      "text": "Back in Kathmandu, I noticed several Swastikas in the streets (on a post, or a little sidewalk temple). I looked into it, and apparently that's an ancient religious symbol in Hinduism, Buddhism, and Jainism. The right facing swastika represents prosperity, good luck, cosmic order in Hinduism and the left-facing one represents universal harmony, eternity in Buddhism, far from what it's associated with now.",
      "type": "text"
    },
